  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "New benchmarks test structure predictors against glycan poses, NMR chemical shifts and disordered-protein ensembles, locating where static models fall short.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is evaluating predicted structures against criteria beyond static fold accuracy. CARVE introduces glycan-specific pose-quality scoring using oRMSD, irRMSD and Fnat with DP-scaled thresholds, benchmarked on 1,974 protein-glycan complexes. A curated NMR backbone 15N chemical-shift dataset benchmarks protein foundation models and finds the largest errors in core residues with fast dynamics, which it follows up with MD analysis. The bAIes framework is extended to six predictors (AlphaFold2/3, Boltz-1/2, ESMFold, ESMFold2) to build atomic-resolution IDP ensembles assessed by inter-residue distance distributions. ProtFlap adds residue-level flexibility prediction from static structures via atomic energy networks trained on RMSF labels. Peripheral items cover coarse-grained mapping choices for ML protein models, 2D interface atlases (TopoPPI) and AlphaFold-supported NCF1 autoinhibition. What is new is the emphasis on dynamics- and chemistry-aware references as test sets. The items report no unified cross-method ranking, so the contribution lies mainly in evaluation design and datasets.",
